<!--Render Target Documentation — Introduction
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.Introduction-->
<rdoc:Introduction xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Purpose and place of the MachineBlocks SCAD render target
  </is>
  <documentation>
    This target serializes MBOM blocks into MachineBlocks V3 SCAD files.
    It is a product render target, separate from @machineblocks/core and from
    the BlockML toolchain targets (blockdoc, xsd, fatblock).

    @machineblocks/core holds the domain BML, documentation, the SCAD runtime
    (lib/block.scad and related files), and example pairs such as
    com.machineblocks.bml.examples.Cross with
    blocks/com/machineblocks/scad/examples/Cross.scad. This package reads that
    library; it does not vendor it.

    Output is MachineBlocks World interpretation: SCAD mb_block() calls. That is
    not a BlockML platform rule. Other targets may emit React, KiCad, or Python
    with no block concept. Mapping used here:

    - BML NativeBlock — mb_block() at the leaf (explicit 1:1)
    - BML composition — nested mb_block() tree
    - Domain types such as Wall — lowered to mb_block() settings
    - BML Set — STEPS array plus view submodules

    All MBOM-to-SCAD mappings are declarative. Processors do not hardcode
    parameter inventories. Native parameters come from NativeBlock.bml.

    The target is browser and Node compatible. No Node-only APIs.
    Host entry for users is @machineblocks/cli.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:V1Scope" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:Introduction>
